## Overview

This project helps users understand telecom plans, customer offerings, and service trade-offs by combining:

- knowledge from telecom plan data
- local vector-based retrieval
- AI evaluation of learner answers
- clear explanations and evidence snippets

It is designed as a lightweight learning demo and portfolio-ready AI project.

## Why this project matters

Telecom onboarding and service learning usually involve product complexity and a large amount of domain knowledge. This project simplifies that by giving users a guided feedback loop:

1. ask a meaningful telecom question
2. retrieve relevant context from plan data
3. evaluate the learner response
4. explain the correct concept
5. reinforce understanding with evidence snippets

## Features

- Telecom quiz generation from plan data
- Answer evaluation with AI-assisted feedback
- Context-aware retrieval from plan knowledge
- Fast local fallback when OpenAI is unavailable
- Clean browser-based learning UI
- Easy setup for local development

## System Architecture

```mermaid
flowchart LR
    A[Telecom plan data] --> B[Knowledge loader]
    B --> C[Vector DB builder]
    C --> D[Quiz question]
    D --> E[User answer]
    E --> F[Retrieval layer]
    F --> G[LLM evaluation or local fallback]
    G --> H[Score + explanation + snippets]
    H --> I[Web UI]
```

## Data Flow

```text
1. Load telecom plan details from JSON
2. Build in-memory document embeddings
3. Select a quiz question
4. Capture the learner answer
5. Retrieve relevant context
6. Evaluate using LLM or local logic
7. Render score, feedback, and evidence
```

